(
 'Reports the status from Git''s perspective.'
 ''
 'By default a short report is returned as a matrix with four columns:'
 ''
 '  [;1] Status info for the index (staging) area'
 '  [;2] Status info for the working area'
 '  [;3] File names relative to the project''s root'
 '  [;4] APL names, if any'
 ''
 'With -noAPLnames the fourth column is omitted, leaving three columns.'
 ''
 'Git reports a folder that is entirely new as a single entry, without naming the files'
 'within it. With -allUntracked those files are reported instead.'
 ''
 '-verbose      : Print a long report instead of returning the matrix'
 '-view         : Put the result into ⎕ED and return ⍬'
 '-noAPLnames   : Suppress the fourth column with the APL names; ignored with -verbose'
 '-allUntracked : Report the files within an untracked folder rather than just the folder'
 ''
 'For more information (particularly the meaning of "status info"):'
 ']APLGit2.Status -???'
)
